virglrenderer: Venus ends an app's context before Metal ends QEMU on too many passes

What: vkr counts the Metal passes (render encoders) each command buffer opens: a clear of
an image (one per level of its ranges; the layers of a level, and a 3D level's depth
slices, are one layered pass), a render pass begin and each next subpass, a dynamic
rendering begin, a blit or resolve region (counted to be safe), on KosmicKrisp a barrier
inside a pass (it splits a multisampled pass there; vkr does not keep the pass's
samples, so every in-pass barrier counts there), the draws that split a pass, and the
secondaries a primary executes (their passes each time). Draws that split a pass: on
both drivers each tessellated draw, and a sample-location or attachment-location change
inside a pass (the pipeline's or a command's); on KosmicKrisp a draw call it unrolls or
predicates in a compute pass first: triangle fans, 8-bit indices, strips with 8- or
16-bit indices and restart off, list restart with primitiveTopologyListRestart, a Flat
fragment input with the last vertex provoking, conditional rendering, and index
robustness (a NULL index buffer, or with robustBufferAccess2 or pipelineRobustness an
indirect or over-reading indexed draw). For that vkr keeps each graphics pipeline's
topology, restart, provoking mode, tessellation and Flat use (the SPIR-V scan; pipeline
libraries merged) and the recording's dynamic state and index buffer. A command buffer
may open 16384 (OMACVM_VENUS_ENCODER_CAP, tests only); a MoltenVK batch (all command
buffers of one VkSubmitInfo or VkSubmitInfo2) twice that. The command past it is refused
before the driver gets it, and the app's context ends with a log line (the guest
recorded and submitted without waiting: it sees a lost device). Other draws, copies,
fills, updates, timestamps and attachment clears do not count.
Why: Metal ends the process (SIGABRT: "Failed to allocate IOGPUDeviceShmem" in
IOGPUMetalCommandBufferStorageGrowKernelCommandBuffer, from AGX::RenderContext::
beginRenderPass) when one Metal command buffer has about 98304 passes. One guest program
ended QEMU and the VM so, with no submit on KosmicKrisp: probes through vkr's dispatch
on the M1 Max (macOS 27, the 3.2.18 drivers, work/v624-hostmem): KosmicKrisp aborted
while recording past 98304 clears of one level (run7-9; 90000 with 150000 asked), past
98304 empty passes (run10), between 90112 and 98304 in-pass barriers of a 4x pass,
between 6144 and 6656 clears of 15 levels, and between 73728 and 81920 triangle fan
draws in one pass (fix/out-B); fans, 8-bit indices, 16-bit strips without restart, list
restart, flat with the last vertex, tessellation, predicates and color-map or
sample-location changes cost 24-113 KB per draw while recording (a pass about 7 KB, a
plain draw 0.1 KB: fix/out-A). 1M plain draws, 204800 copies, 204800 1x in-pass
barriers, 200 clears of 2048 layers, 16384 clears of a 2048-deep 3D image and 65536
blits or resolves did not abort on KosmicKrisp. MoltenVK aborted at the encode: with
prefill at vkEndCommandBuffer after 150000 clears, 204800 passes, renderings, blits or
resolves, and 114688 tessellated draws or draws with a color-map or sample-location
change each; without prefill at vkQueueSubmit of one batch of 8 x 16384 clears (4 x
16384 in one batch, 8 batches of 16384 and 8 submits went through). KosmicKrisp took
8 x 16384 in one batch and 16 live command buffers of 16384 each (also over 2
contexts). 16384 is 6x below the clear abort and 4.5x below the fan-draw abort; a Zink
frame has about 2000 passes. On the mini's M4 (fix-700 r2) KosmicKrisp aborted between
74752 and 75264 clears of one level, 4.6x above the cap. An 8 GB Mac is not measured (the
cap stays fixed).
Upstream: OmacVM policy; nothing posted.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (the h-pass- cases: the legal maximum and one
past it per kind at a cap of 1024, the default cap, 100000 clears that ended the process
before, levels, layers, 3D clears, secondaries, a real MoltenVK batch, and the
h-pass-draw- cases: each draw kind that splits a pass past the cap, the ones that do not
within it).

